1,10$ genus Dendrominia Ghobad-Nejhad & Duhem gen. nov. ...
1,0$ source :/// Novelties in the Corticiales: Vuilleminia nilsii sp. nov. and Dendrominia gen. nov. (Basidiomycota) /// Masoomeh Ghobad-Nejhad • Bernard Duhem- Mycological Progress_13-1_2014 
1,0$
1,0 $ Basidiocarp conspicuous, in small patches resembling  a typical Dendrothele; basidiospores allantoid;  hyphae with clamps $ D. dryina
1,2 $ Basidiocarp very thin, confluent, inconspicuous;  basidiospores lunate, bent characteristically in the middle;  hyphae with or without clamps
2,0 $ Hyphae with clamps; basidiocarp on decorticated  wood $ D. ericae
2,0 $ Hyphae without clamps; basidiocarp on bark $ D. maculata

Dendrominia Ghobad-Nejhad & Duhem gen. nov.
10,0$Diagnosis Dendrominia is characterized by a resupinate and smooth basidiocarp, monomitic hyphal system with or without clamps, with fine amorphous crystals on hyphae, large, cylindrical-clavate basidia with four sterigmata, lack of cystidia, presence of dendrohyphidia, and lunate to allantoid basidiospores.///Dendrominia differs from Vuilleminia by its basidiocarp texture (ceraceous to crustaceous in the former, mostly gelatinous in the latter) and lack of clamp in some of its species.///Etymology Dendrominia, a combination from the generic names Dendrothele and Vuilleminia.///Typus Dendrominia maculata (H.S. Jacks. & P.A. Lemke) Ghobad-Nejhad & Duhem comb. nov. = Vuilleminia corticola Parm. Eesti NSV Tead. Akad